  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** First-quarter revenue declined but adjusted EBITDA held flat, while orders came in strong with a book-to-bill above 1.0. This points to a growing backlog and improving demand in the company’s energy-related end markets, even as near-term product shipments remained soft. The recent IPO and capital raise support the business as it navigates a mixed operating environment transitioning toward higher activity.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management completed the IPO in April 2026, raising substantial net proceeds to fortify the balance sheet. They issued full-year adjusted EBITDA guidance, signaling confidence in converting the order backlog into improved profitability. Analysts responded with a consensus Buy rating and initiation of coverage by major firms, reflecting early credibility in leadership’s strategy and post-IPO execution.",
